I recently uploaded version 1.5 of my GameBoy advance game AGB_Hack.
This release includes a new graphical tile mode and minimap (both on
by default, but text mode is still available).

http://www.freewebs.com/drussell/Download.htm#GameBoyAdvance

AGB_Hack is adapted from Don Kneller's PC Hack 3.61, which was
released about a year before the first public version of NetHack.
Unlike PC Hack, AGB_Hack is largely menu-driven, but there is also a
virtual keyboard that simulates the old input system. Another major
difference is that, due to the very limited memory of the GBA,
AGB_Hack must save games as a sequence of keystrokes. To return to a
previously saved game, it must be automatically played back from the
beginning, which can take as long as five minutes for a long
recording. This has the side effect of allowing players to hack the
saved data to undo missteps, but it is also very useful for debugging.

